00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
m 0 0 l 102 0 l 102 58 l 0 58

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
m 0 0 l 102 0 l 102 58 l 0 58

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
m 0 0 l 102 0 l 102 58 l 0 58

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
<b></b>Kahvel

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
<b></b><u>\h\hTokitate Yuka\h\h</u>

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
<b></b><u>Yotsuya Yuusuke</u>

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.010
\h\hFollow the Deokk soldiers\h\h

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.640
If we stay on the main road,

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.060
we should come across a 
settlement eventually.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:50.020
And if we offer to escort any 
deliveries from there to Radodorbo,

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.990
we can achieve our goal.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:55.660
Yeah, and to do that, we might 
not even need a settlement.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.500
We could run into a traveling 
merchant headed for Radodorbo.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.900
Oh, yeah, and escorting them 
would have the same effect.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.120
This might actually be easy.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.040
Looks like Team A is making good progress.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.250
So as Team B, we'll also follow the plan

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.060
to continue pursuing the route 
Deokk's wagon is taking.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.690
<i>Why am I on this team?</i>

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.080
<i>It's bound to be a lot more dangerous!</i>

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.540
They don't know that we 
made it out of the cave.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.390
Killing them in an ambush 
might work well enough,

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.200
but one thing concerns me.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.190
Before they locked us in that cave...

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.640
We're counting on you.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.540
I suspect it was routine communication 
with the kingdom...

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.880
but it was likely a notice that they 
were going to trap some enemy heroes

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.820
and soldiers of Cortonel the next day.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.960
There's a good chance you're right.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.830
And what if the kingdom's 
soldiers went missing

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.970
shortly after trapping Cortonel's soldiers?

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.190
It might imply that we escaped their trap

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:24.290
and ended up killing them?

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.350
Right.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.690
No, they are a militant nation.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:30.450
Regardless of the truth,

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.260
they might use it as an 
excuse to declare war.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.870
We must avoid that.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.510
You mean war would break out?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.070
Speaking strictly in terms of numbers,

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.150
the kingdom has ten times 
the soldiers we do.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.680
We'd stand no chance...

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.300
and I don't want to see my country 
destroyed because of me.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.580
So what we need to do first

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:57.530
is get them to write a letter 
saying Cortonel isn't the enemy.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.370
Get <i>them</i> to write that?

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:02.990
We don't know his written language, 
penmanship, or signature,

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:07.360
so we can't force them to write 
it, or write it for them.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.880
We need to convince them 
that it's the truth

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.280
so that they'll report it to the kingdom.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.950
Uh, that sounds impossible.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.640
<i>A letter might not have any effect.</i>

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:23.330
<i>The kingdom could just ignore the letter 
and start a war with Cortonel.</i>

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.000
<i>But still,</i>

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.680
<i>I want them to know hell and despair...</i>

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.290
<i>humiliation and regret...</i>

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.550
<i>and I want them feeling 
all that as they die.</i>

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.860
I have an idea.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.400
<i>What an evil face!</i>

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.140
We finally caught up to them.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:54.450
Looks like the soldiers and the 
convicts are all unharmed.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.960
When do we strike?

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.020
Not yet.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.620
This is all flat land with no obstacles.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:03.820
We'll follow them at a fixed distance 
until everything is ready.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.000
Go time will be tomorrow.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.760
Okay, got it.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:18.690
You know, I'm impressed you keep coming 
up with these ruthless ideas.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:23.090
Maybe the plan wasn't to make 
you a hero, but a demon king.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:27.530
Well, I was always good 
at stuff like that...

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:32.010
Like the <i>Dark Surreal</i> series 
and the <i>Fall Bad</i> series.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.010
Ah, console games, huh?

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:39.120
Thinking about how to kill enemies 
is a pretty regular part of my day.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.790
I haven't played anything but social 
network games for about a year now.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:47.410
<i>Your smile is more beautiful than 
any treasure in the world.</i>

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:45.440
God, I wanna meet Tsubasa-kun right now!

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.730
Tsubasa-kyun! Want!

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.530
So this world...

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.020
This world is virtual, right?

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.880
I'm not really sure.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:00.010
So let's say...

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:07.280
I-If you... kissed a character 
from this world...

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.690
would it count as your first kiss?

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:11.620
Huh?

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.980
Wait a minute... Don't tell me...

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.120
Did you?! Who was it? Makuah-san?

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:23.080
Hell no! I wasn't talking about me!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:23.940
Huh?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.540
Shindou-san, then?

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.500
It was just hypothetical!

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.710
It wasn't about anyone in particular!

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:35.390
<i>I meant you! Also, you're just 
naturally rude, aren't you?!</i>

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:39.700
Yeah, but isn't a first kiss 
just an abstract concept?

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:43.100
So why not count it toward your 
experience, virtual or not?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.570
Especially in a world as 
realistic as this one.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.720
Anyway, I'm gonna swap out with Kahvel-san.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.610
<i>And what would it be if you were asleep?</i>

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.550
<i>I guess it wouldn't count 
toward your experience, then.</i>

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.910
<i>I mean, I've seen a lot of 
stories where the person</i>

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:03.410
<i>was actually awake and just missed the 
right timing to pretend to wake up...</i>

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.410
Kahvel-san, rise and shine.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.830
It's your turn to take over the watch.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.830
<i>But based on that reaction,</i>

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.210
<i>he was legit asleep.</i>

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.390
It has been a difficult journey.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:15.830
All of our senior officers died in action,

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:20.040
leaving me, a lower officer, 
to lead the remainder of our march,

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:22.810
in an unprecedented turn of events.

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:26.080
However, our journey will 
end in three days.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.610
By giving these heretics 
practicing a foreign religion

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.450
their execution in the international 
port town of Radodorbo,

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.460
we can eliminate them at the source

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:40.120
and stop them from contaminating our 
continent of Meri any further!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.500
Yeah!

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.270
So, hey...

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.280
Got a minute?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:48.670
What?!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.610
You made it out of that dungeon?!

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:52.880
Prepare for battle!

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:56.040
Now, hang on a minute.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.440
I'm just here to negotiate.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.160
Negotiate?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:00.900
Yeah.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.440
You know fighting won't do 
any good anyway, right?

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:08.280
We heroes recover from any 
wound in twenty seconds,

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.100
and even if we die, 
we revive in forty seconds.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.080
You guys can't beat us.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.170
What is it, then? 
What do you want to negotiate?

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.010
First, one thing...

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:23.120
The four from Cortonel died in that cave.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.960
Also, two of the heroes fell in a hole,

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.470
so only the four-eyes and I remain.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.910
Yo, four-eyes!

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:32.080
Keep your damn voice down. I'm right here.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.220
This negotiation only stands 
to benefit you, anyway.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.270
Why do I need to be here?

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.630
Only him?

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.070
Yeah!

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:44.970
He's a hero, but he converted 
to the religion of Arteros!

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:46.380
What?!

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:47.570
That's right.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:52.180
I'm negotiating for my 
three fellow believers.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.960
If you don't hand them over,

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.810
I'll use my immortality to spread our 
Saint's teachings all over the world!

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.950
The people will heed the words of a hero!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:01.980
And then...

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.700
the world will be teeming 
with believers of Arteros!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.070
Even if we comply, 
you'll still be free to do that!

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:10.380
What is there to negotiate?!

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:14.550
You have until the sun 
rises tomorrow to decide.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:18.270
If the three believers are hurt or 
killed before then, the deal is off.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.760
I will return here at that time.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.580
You'd better make your decision by then.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.400
So long! Let's go, four-eyes!

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.700
Oh, shut up!

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:38.370
What should we do?

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.160
There's nothing to negotiate!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.280
But we can't just do nothing...

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.830
I realize that.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:47.220
If an immortal hero propagates 
that heretical religion,

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:51.270
this expedition will be not 
only wasted, but detrimental!

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.470
We must do something about them.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.370
But wait...

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:57.100
He said they've already lost two heroes!

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.290
That's it!

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:01.860
Heroes can't die, but they can be 
trapped in holes or jail cells!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:05.330
Yes, so if we capture them before 
the end of the night—

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.700
Good point.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.740
Heroes don't die, but that's all.

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.240
Yeah, hi! Four-eyes here!

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:14.820
Y—

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:15.650
You!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.740
Shh! I came here in secret.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:19.650
What do you want?

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:24.330
You know I've never really gotten 
along with that jerk, right?

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.300
Y-Yes...

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:29.170
Come to think of it, you didn't 
seem fond of each other.

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.240
What, then? Are you selling him out?

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:33.730
Now that it's just the two of us,

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.660
it's been even worse than before.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.750
If you're willing to capture him, 
I'll tell you where he sleeps.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:43.590
How about it? You could leave right now.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.380
We can't trust you.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:49.640
You're probably planning to free the 
convicts while we're away from the wagon.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:54.030
Then why don't you come with me 
first to see where he's sleeping?

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:57.950
No, going there and coming 
back first would waste time.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.050
What should we do, then?

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.780
Hem and I will go and capture him.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:04.560
Gurobi, stay and keep watch.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:05.370
Yes, sir!

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.650
If she's lying, we'll just take her prisoner.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:09.780
All right?

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:12.420
Of course. Let me show you the way.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:14.760
<i>Two against one, huh?</i>

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.090
<i>Oh, boy. They fell for it.</i>

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.590
Bring me a rope.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.500
At once, sir!

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.890
<i>Don't blame me.</i>

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.010
m 0 0 l 258 0 l 258 200 l 0 200

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.010
[Attacks on Humans]

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.010
If a player attacks a human, it is considered
unjustifiable self-defense against humans.
(This is not the case if the human attacks the
player first.)

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.840
Well? How much longer?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.700
It's just up ahead.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.650
We'll be there in another minute or so.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.770
Very well. One minute, then.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.320
And now?

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.600
Soon.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.190
We'll be there in about thirty seconds.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:55.080
Hem, go take a look.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:55.960
Yes, sir.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:02.820
Well, I've probably dragged 
them far enough away.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:06.540
Captain...

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.000
I didn't see anything up ahead.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:14.930
So you <i>were</i> lying.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:16.660
When we reach Radodorbo,

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.920
I'll tie weights to you and 
throw you into the sea!

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.370
You can spend eternity there!

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:23.870
What's that?

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:29.410
Welcome back...

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.820
and I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.790
You two are hereby relieved of duty.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.710
Return to your homeland.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:43.660
The Arteros believers...

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:47.670
Did you kill them?! Even the child?!

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.220
You look so confused!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.940
The part about Kahvel-san 
and her two men dying

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:00.700
and the other two heroes falling 
in a hole was true...

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:05.530
but everything from Yotsuya-kun's 
conversion to Arteros onward was a lie!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:06.560
What?!

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.750
You see...

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:11.750
We're only here to mess with 
you in the name of revenge.

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:16.930
For our five fallen allies.

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:21.010
Now, the last survivor...

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:23.430
S-Stop it! Stop!

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.970
This is the end for the missionary.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.200
He soaked him in oil?!

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.010
He's burning him alive!

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:37.560
While I'm at it...

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:40.930
I think I'll set your 
horse's ass on fire, too!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.150
What?!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.120
We must go after—

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.670
No, if we leave the heroes here alone...

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:54.660
Burn through it!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.580
Majiha Fire!

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.140
You won't get away!

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.460
<b>Wizard Ring</b>

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.460
<b>Wizard Staff (Heat)</b>

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.460
<b>Wizard (Heat) Clothes (Top)</b>

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.460
<b>Wizard (Heat) Boots</b>

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.460
<b>Wizard (Heat) Socks</b>

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.230
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:11.370
Damn it!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.690
That's hot!

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.960
Our horse!

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:24.100
Maybe we'll take what's in the wagon, too!

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.660
Try and catch us!

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.100
After them!

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.500
Are they coming?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.040
They sure are.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.630
It'd be all over if they 
checked the bodies, huh?

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:48.270
Sir, there seems to be quite 
a lot of noise outside.

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:50.340
What's going on?

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:53.860
The hero?!

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.200
Take off your clothes! Hurry!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:56.010
Huh?!

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:59.000
We're going to save you.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:04.500
Perfect.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.940
Now they'll write that Kahvel-san and 
the others from Cortonel are dead,

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:14.690
and that we heroes interfered 
with them to get revenge.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.920
So the relationship between Cortonel and 
Deokk will remain unchanged, at least.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.420
In fact, Kamilto...

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:25.300
<i>Our refusal to let them accompany us</i>

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.500
<i>and trapping them in the 
ruins led us to this!</i>

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.080
<i>I can't face King Deokk now!</i>

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:37.330
...is drowning in despair over his 
own lapse in judgment right now.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:40.100
<i>I'm not sure if I should be impressed...</i>

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.420
<i>He's definitely not the kind 
of guy I'd want as a friend.</i>

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:46.600
<i>I'd want him as an enemy even less, though.</i>

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:55.960
It's been three days and we haven't 
come across a single wagon.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:59.630
If we follow the main road, 
we're sure to find a settlement.

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:02.680
And if we find one, 
we're sure to find merchants, too.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:08.470
Even if we do, there's no guarantee 
we'll find cargo bound for Radodorbo.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:12.060
Four days and three hours left...

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:16.410
I hope everything's going 
okay for the other two.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:26.440
I found a cave down there.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.940
Oh! Great Heroes!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:35.330
Hey, I see the boy regained consciousness.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.250
Yes, just now.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.440
So, um...

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.050
Belili-kun, right?

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:43.160
Yes, that's right.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.690
They told me you saved my life.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:48.060
Thank you so much,

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.790
pretty hero lady!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:00.150
W-Well, you're very welcome!

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:10.100
Okay, just calm down!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.270
I am <i>not</i> into all that shota stuff!

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:20.120
<i>But man... I never imagined 
that plan would really work.</i>

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:24.530
What we'll need in advance is 
dolls to represent three people.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:28.690
We can sew together cloth sacks and 
unused clothing to make them.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:30.950
But if they look at the faces, 
they'll know they're fake.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.850
We'll make it look like we 
put bags over their heads.

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.110
Then, if we tie ropes around their necks...

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.060
It'll look like we hanged them.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:40.300
Uh...

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.420
If we can mix a real human in with them,

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:46.310
it'll make these bodies look more real...

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.560
I understand your plan.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.530
I must prepare for departure.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:00.630
But if we do this, won't it mean 
killing a human character for real?

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.220
You haven't actually done that 
all this time, have you?

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:08.160
Yeah, I'm a little worried about how 
much it'll affect my experience...

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.970
No, that's not my point.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:15.010
I mean... do you really think 
this world is a game?

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.520
If it's real, wouldn't that be really bad?

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:19.190
Well... I guess?

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:24.220
I mean, yeah, if it's a game, the AI they 
gave the NPCs is insanely advanced...

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.160
But look at us.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:31.350
See? We have a sense of pain, 
but we barely feel any.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:37.020
I don't know if it's just futuristic 
technology, like the Game Master said,

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:42.070
but ultimately, it's well-made enough 
that we'd mistake it for reality.

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:47.480
I mean, we can pull weapons and 
armor out of thin air, too.

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:51.030
Isn't that enough to convince 
you that it's not real?

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:55.620
Well... not like it matters to me, 
since I'm not the one who'll be doing it...

00:19:56.870 --> 00:20:01.350
Okay, we achieved our goal 
of rescuing the prisoners.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:04.450
Now if Kahvel-san can pull 
off her part of the plan,

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:07.450
we can avoid war, just like she wanted.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:08.520
Hey...

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:13.020
Even if this is a virtual game world,

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.890
is it really worth killing 
someone to stop a war?

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:17.880
That's even more reason to do it.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:20.930
It'll be the same world from the 
fifth quest stage onward, you know.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:26.260
And more importantly, it was a request 
from a friend. Who could refuse?

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.050
Huh?

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:29.200
What? You do realize...

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.280
one of our friends was already killed.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.190
So wouldn't you kill his killer?

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:34.780
What?!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:41.230
Whoa! You're the last person I want to hear 
that kind of friends-first logic from!

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:46.200
I mean... if someone killed my favorite 
character in one of my games,

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.560
I'd totally kill whoever killed them...

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.720
But if that's how you feel...

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:54.400
What are the three of us to you?

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.450
What do you mean?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.400
Like... say there's a bus.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.600
A bus?

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:03.030
It's about to fall off a cliff,

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.660
and depending on how the weight of 
the passengers is distributed,

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.710
it'll fall and they'll all die.

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:11.020
We just happen to be four 
of those passengers.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:12.960
That analogy sucks!

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.280
It's exactly like that, though!

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:18.590
Tokitate-san, are you forgetting 
that your own life is on the line?

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:27.930
I'm saying we can't afford to 
worry ourselves over the lives

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:29.760
of characters in a game.

